## Journey A — Local AI

1. Install an approved local model.
2. Disconnect external networking.
3. Start real local inference.
4. Verify streaming.
5. Verify model attribution.
6. Verify no cloud request occurred in local-only mode.

## Journey B — Cloud AI

1. Configure an approved cloud provider.
2. Verify credentials.
3. Perform real inference.
4. Verify model attribution.
5. Revoke credentials.
6. Verify truthful failure handling.

## Journey C — Google Drive

1. Authorize a test Google account.
2. Select a non-sensitive document.
3. Download/export.
4. Parse and index it.
5. Retrieve its content.
6. Verify exact citation.
7. Modify the document.
8. Verify synchronization.
9. Revoke access and verify appropriate exclusion.

## Journey D — Knowledge and Memory

1. Approve a memory.
2. Verify provenance.
3. Retrieve it in a new session.
4. Edit it.
5. Export it.
6. Delete it.
7. Verify deletion from applicable derived indexes and caches.
8. Test cross-project isolation.

## Journey E — Sandbox

1. Create an isolated environment.
2. Run harmless test code.
3. Verify isolation.
4. Test restricted network.
5. Trigger resource limits.
6. Cancel a job.
7. Generate file diffs.
8. Approve delivery.
9. Verify the original project.
10. Test rollback.

